{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies","id":929259,"title":"Upcoming 2E Legacies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-10T10:05:05-07:00","id":929259,"title":"Upcoming 2E Legacies","content":"Hi! I tried to search in the forums, but no luck. Does anybody know what are the next Legacies DaveB will redesign from its 1st edition version in blogs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:57:25-07:00","id":929344,"title":"","content":"Sisterhood of the Blessed (Ladder or Seers / Acanthus)<br /> Eleventh Question (Guardian or Mysterium / Moros) <b>- already in the corebook</b><br /> Perfected Adept (Arrow or Council / Obrimos)<br /> Cryptologos (Council or Mysterium / Mastigos)<br /> Orphans of Proteus (Mysterium or Arrow / Thyrsus)<br /> <br /> The Adepts, Sisterhood and Cryptologos are all back-of-beermat converted already for my own game, as they're the Legacies my players' characters have taken. The Redoubtable Neall Raemonn Price is working up the Orphans as a hobby project.<br /> <br /> Bonus round, for if we find ourselves overburdened with time, will be:<br /> <br /> House of Ariadne (Mysterium or Seers / Acanthus)<br /> Forge Masters (Arrow or Council / Moros)<br /> Clavicularius / Bene Ashmedai (Ladder or Seers / Mastigos)<br /> Dreamspeakers (Council / Thyrsus)<br /> Daksha (Mysterium or Guardian / Obrimos)<br /> <br /> Although they will have to wait until after Signs of Sorcery comes out - the Clavicularius and Forge Masters in particular have Attainments based on spells from that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 07-10-2016, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T14:42:51-07:00","id":929392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=929344#post929344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sisterhood of the Blessed (Ladder or Seers / Acanthus)<br /> Eleventh Question (Guardian or Mysterium / Moros) <b>- already in the corebook</b><br /> Perfected Adept (Arrow or Council / Obrimos)<br /> Cryptologos (Council or Mysterium / Mastigos)<br /> Orphans of Proteus (Mysterium or Arrow / Thyrsus)<br /> <br /> The Adepts, Sisterhood and Cryptologos are all back-of-beermat converted already for my own game, as they're the Legacies my players' characters have taken. The Redoubtable Neall Raemonn Price is working up the Orphans as a hobby project.<br /> <br /> Bonus round, for if we find ourselves overburdened with time, will be:<br /> <br /> House of Ariadne (Mysterium or Seers / Acanthus)<br /> Forge Masters (Arrow or Council / Moros)<br /> Clavicularius / Bene Ashmedai (Ladder or Seers / Mastigos)<br /> Dreamspeakers (Council / Thyrsus)<br /> Daksha (Mysterium or Guardian / Obrimos)<br /> <br /> Although they will have to wait until after Signs of Sorcery comes out - the Clavicularius and Forge Masters in particular have Attainments based on spells from that book.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what's the deal with making almost all of the Legacies have two Orders? I do get a few of them, like the Eleventh Question, Cryptologos, Forge Masters, and all of the &quot;or Seers&quot; ones barring the House of Ariadne. On the other hand, some just really don't make sense to me, and feel kind of arbitrary; I mean, what's especially Libertine about the Perfected Adepts that makes the Free Council a Parent Order along with the Arrow over any of the other Orders? Or what's so Guardian-y about the Daksha? Or Mysterium-y/Arrow-y about the Orphans of Proteus?<br /> <br /> Now, I fully understand that any Legacy's doctrine can mesh well with that of any Order, but I believe a Legacy's Parent Order(s) should be exemplary matches with the Legacy, and not just OK fits, which is what's weirding me out by some of the above choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T15:40:46-07:00","id":929420,"title":"","content":"Perfected Adept FC: Probably buying into the idea of bodily perfectionists, the wave of crossfit and new age means of reaching satisfaction if not enlightenment with your body.<br /> <br /> Daksha Guardians: They're basically racist against non-transgender, especially Sleepers, and the Guardians have a kind of split, on the one hand they have to protect Sleepers on the other their lives would have less hassles if they didn't need to protect them so assiduously.<br /> <br /> Orphans of Proteus Mysterium: The Mysterium want to explore the limits of the world via magic and the place of magic in the world and Orphans let them either blend in and minimize the observer effect or experience the outlandish strangeness of being some other kind of species, mineral, etc and apply their magical insight.<br /> <br /> That's just off the top of my head really rough idea, but anyways, since any Mage from anywhere can join a legacy is they can make a Praxis that the first attainment can be based on then it makes sense that people from multiple Orders might show an interest. Being an exemplary match doesn't have much to do with it, as long as you can manage to make yourself an ideological match somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T16:32:17-07:00","id":929446,"title":"","content":"Praxis way is superior anyway, because it gives you beats. Which isn't bad, because it makes sense even appropiate Orders and Paths can and often will train for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T17:19:12-07:00","id":929460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=929344#post929344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sisterhood of the Blessed (Ladder or Seers / Acanthus)<br /> Clavicularius / Bene Ashmedai (Ladder or Seers / Mastigos)</div> </div> </div> </div>Are the Clavicularius and the Bene Ashmedai possibilities for both the Ladder and the Seers or does this imply that the former is a Ladder Legacy and the latter a Seers one?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T18:18:42-07:00","id":929473,"title":"","content":"They're both eligible for either the Ladder or the Seers. Legacies have an unnerving tendency to cross-pollinate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T21:23:32-07:00","id":929542,"title":"","content":"In truth the Free Council would fit for any legacy, they are far from a homogenized group easily containing militant groups, social oriented groups and mystics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T22:25:25-07:00","id":929559,"title":"","content":"This is much, much better than I thought about. I'm really looking forward to Round 1 Legacies, but especially to Round 2 Legacies! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T22:30:20-07:00","id":929562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=929344#post929344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sisterhood of the Blessed (Ladder or Seers / Acanthus)<br /> Eleventh Question (Guardian or Mysterium / Moros) <b>- already in the corebook</b><br /> Perfected Adept (Arrow or Council / Obrimos)<br /> Cryptologos (Council or Mysterium / Mastigos)<br /> Orphans of Proteus (Mysterium or Arrow / Thyrsus)<br /> <br /> The Adepts, Sisterhood and Cryptologos are all back-of-beermat converted already for my own game, as they're the Legacies my players' characters have taken. The Redoubtable Neall Raemonn Price is working up the Orphans as a hobby project.<br /> <br /> Bonus round, for if we find ourselves overburdened with time, will be:<br /> <br /> House of Ariadne (Mysterium or Seers / Acanthus)<br /> Forge Masters (Arrow or Council / Moros)<br /> Clavicularius / Bene Ashmedai (Ladder or Seers / Mastigos)<br /> Dreamspeakers (Council / Thyrsus)<br /> Daksha (Mysterium or Guardian / Obrimos)<br /> <br /> Although they will have to wait until after Signs of Sorcery comes out - the Clavicularius and Forge Masters in particular have Attainments based on spells from that book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, these are Legacies I'm steering clear of, now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I can get to work doing my conversions for a few others from 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T23:23:13-07:00","id":929582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=929392#post929392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, what's especially Libertine about the Perfected Adepts that makes the Free Council a Parent Order along with the Arrow over any of the other Orders?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd wager that the legacy's ties to &quot;chi&quot; and other concepts in traditional Chinese medicine are what associate it with the Free Council. I figure the writeup will mention something about one of the Nameless orders that founded the Perfected Adepts going on to found the Free Council, or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 07-11-2016, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T05:10:57-07:00","id":929662,"title":"","content":"Daksha Guardians? I'm profoundly disturbed just by reading these two words together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T08:47:57-07:00","id":929758,"title":"","content":"While I agree on general direction with coming of Two Parent Orders ( I'm the one proposing to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/884775-2e-fan-uncrowned-kings\">remake Uncrowned Kings in to Silver Ladder and Free Council group</a> ), I'm a bit worried that it seems like (almost) <i>every</i> Legacy now have dual Orders, even those not meshing good in two groups.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm always assumed that every Pentacle group can have Seers of Throne faction, so I even did not count them as Parent Order...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T09:05:06-07:00","id":929771,"title":"","content":"Why? Having a standard design formula (&quot;there are always 2 Orders, 1 Path, and a Praxis methods of entrance&quot;) is a good, consolidated approach that keeps thing consistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T09:09:45-07:00","id":929776,"title":"","content":"Above lists seems like putting Seers is more: 'We do not have idea what second Pentacle Order would work in this example - Okay, we must put second Order, so it will be Seers'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or things like Guardian Dakasha.<br /> <br /> <b>I'm all for opening format to second Paret Order - but not making it <i>ironclad</i> standard.</b> And not count Seers in it, as from what I understand setting, Seers can almost always have their own version of any Legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T09:13:56-07:00","id":929781,"title":"","content":"Why do you assume that rewritten Dakasha won't fit Guardians? I mean, I'm usually the bleak, cup-half-shattered-and-filled-with-filth person who looks at everything with gloom and doom in mind, expecting failure everywhere, and yet I see this a good opportunity to make these Legacies more interesting by including 2nd-parent-order elements in them instead of thinking it's just forcing a second tag on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T10:20:10-07:00","id":929805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=929776#post929776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Above lists seems like putting Seers is more: 'We do not have idea what second Pentacle Order would work in this example - Okay, we must put second Order, so it will be Seers'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or things like Guardian Dakasha.<br /> <br /> <b>I'm all for opening format to second Paret Order - but not making it <i>ironclad</i> standard.</b> And not count Seers in it, as from what I understand setting, Seers can almost always have their own version of any Legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You really don't see how the Legacy that uses cities as a divination tool, reading information in subtle patterns isn't appropriate for the Seers? Or the twin &quot;weaponize your own selfishness&quot; goetic ones?<br /> <br /> Pah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T10:25:00-07:00","id":929808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=929805#post929805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really don't see how the Legacy that uses cities as a divination tool, reading information in subtle patterns isn't appropriate for the Seers? Or the twin &quot;weaponize your own selfishness&quot; goetic ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>In almost the same way as <i>any other</i> Legacy can be made into Seers one. It's nothing extraordinary in here. There are only limited number of truly Pentacle Legacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-11-2016, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T11:47:09-07:00","id":929865,"title":"","content":"My first thought with Daksha in the Guardians would be both magically developing new identities and the ties to Sleeper occult societies (ie, Theosophy). The GotV have more going on than just hiding magic, although there could definitely be Daksha who believe in magic being fragile and only for the worthy.<br /> <br /> Very excited to see the Dreamspeakers on the maybe list! Fingers crossed they get covered sometime, they're going to be a big part of the game I'm running in the LA setting and I'd love to see an official in-depth 2E take on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T11:52:48-07:00","id":929868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=929392#post929392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's the deal with making almost all of the Legacies have two Orders? I do get a few of them, like the Eleventh Question, Cryptologos, Forge Masters, and all of the &quot;or Seers&quot; ones barring the House of Ariadne. On the other hand, some just really don't make sense to me, and feel kind of arbitrary; I mean, what's especially Libertine about the Perfected Adepts that makes the Free Council a Parent Order along with the Arrow over any of the other Orders? Or what's so Guardian-y about the Daksha? Or Mysterium-y/Arrow-y about the Orphans of Proteus?<br /> <br /> Now, I fully understand that any Legacy's doctrine can mesh well with that of any Order, but I believe a Legacy's Parent Order(s) should be exemplary matches with the Legacy, and not just OK fits, which is what's weirding me out by some of the above choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the sense that a lot of Legacies were going to be rewritten to open them up to more Orders, which is something I'm really looking forward to, perhaps even moreso than getting their Attainments. There are some Legacies in first edition that are so heavily tied into the culture of one specific Order that I have difficulty seeing why Mages from other Orders would ever be interested in joining them. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:54:53-07:00","id":929912,"title":"","content":"Yeah - bear in mind that some Legacies will end up rather different from their first-edition versions, which is a <i>good</i> thing; the changes to the setting, especially the historicity of it and the clearer post-Order books view of how Mage Society functions, would be short-changed if we just stuck with updating Attainments.<br /> <br /> Look at the Eleventh Question's backstory in 2e compared to the original in Guardians of the Veil.<br /> <br /> In 2e, the House of Ariadne were a Seer Legacy that had a Diamond-based offshoot appear via stolen soul stones. (Why should such things always be portrayed as going the other way? This isn't Masquerade's Antitribu)<br /> <br /> In 2e, the Cryptologos are a Prime Legacy with things like Words of Truth as their Attainments.<br /> <br /> We tried to seed lots of hints into those two-sentence write-ups in the corebook. The Daksha allowing Guardian members is no accident. It just looks weird at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:19:54-07:00","id":929931,"title":"","content":"I understand that a lot of people might be sceptical about thes fluff changes and be &quot;it's perfect as it is, why change&quot;, perceiving it as either a change for a sake of change, or as a net loss, but as someone wise said somewhere - your customers don't know they want change until they get it, and before they get it, they will oppose it with all their strength. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:40:16-07:00","id":929943,"title":"","content":"Let's see:<br /> <br /> Since both Daksha and the Guardians were involved with Theosophist societies, some cross-pollination could have occurred. Daksha sense of superiority and interest in reclaiming Artifacts mesh well with the Inheritor faction. They also try to guide the evolutionary destiny of mankind, which they kinda-sorta have in common with the Messianistic faction. I mean the compounds are already there. If you look at it closely, Guardians and Daksha start to eerily fit together.<br /> <br /> Also, Wyrdhamster's argument was misread. He claims that since Seers have counterparts of most Legacies, specifically stating it is redundant and doesn't look neat on paper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T16:23:05-07:00","id":930023,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that the Daksha had a connection with the Nazis that went off the rails, that could explain a new fear of sleepers learning too much and a new tie to the Guardians.<br /> \u200bPersonally I'm not a big fan of tying legacies to orders, yes some would have commonalities that tend to bring them together, but I always felt legacies should be more personal, less institutional.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T16:36:19-07:00","id":930032,"title":"","content":"Why can't they be both?<br /> <br /> Anyway on some level because of the fact that a legacy requires at the very least the structure of mentor and student (Barring individuals who start their own), and many build into a community of like minds, it's hard to avoid some level of heirarchy inside a legacy and the ones at the top are also likely to have strong ties to their Orders.<br /> <br /> Indeed, founders of legacies would have been members of their Order first and to find pupils they'd be best served looking inside their own Order where prospects have been indoctrinated into similar ideologies and vetted by other members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-11-2016, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T16:54:27-07:00","id":930037,"title":"","content":"Actually, you don't need a student mentor thing if you don't want to. One of reasons why it's a good thing you can learn from a daimonicon or a Soul Stone is that this allows your player to pick their Legacy even without other people of this Legacy being around, as long as they care to somehow get themselves an item to learn from.<br /> <br /> This has interesting consequence in our games, where we rarely see Mages above Gnosis 3, because it turns Soul Stones into crucial learning aid even when you are in a pre-estabilished Legacy with a Mentor around (because Mentor to master 3rd Attainment minimum, and that requires Gnosis 4, which is our &quot;elite of elite&quot; tier of Mages). This results in...interesting dynamics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T17:24:31-07:00","id":930046,"title":"","content":"Technically those are still mentors, they're just the inanimate sort left behind by the living ones. Though yeah, it does enable you to be divorced from the social goings-on of a legacy. My point still stands though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T17:29:29-07:00","id":930050,"title":"","content":"Actually, ignore this, I misremembered it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-11-2016, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T23:49:44-07:00","id":930211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=930023#post930023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that the Daksha had a connection with the Nazis that went off the rails, that could explain a new fear of sleepers learning too much and a new tie to the Guardians.<br /> \u200bPersonally I'm not a big fan of tying legacies to orders, yes some would have commonalities that tend to bring them together, but I always felt legacies should be more personal, less institutional.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with Guardian Daksha is that it's partially diluted themes of Legacy. Daksha were point made that Mysterium are not 'nice guys' that share knowlegde - it shown they ideology lead to Nazis. Now if we made them Guardians it's much less impact of Mysterium's possible 'evilness' as Guardians are known to make really questionable things in first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T00:00:27-07:00","id":930216,"title":"","content":"That sounds like making them multi dimensional, instead of one dimensional, possibly mustache twirling villains.<br /> EDIT<br /> Eh, let's wait until it's written and then judge if it diluted, enhanced, or murdered themes of the Legacy. We are pretty much trying to solve the mystery without even letting author lay out the clues, and calling the solution bad already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-12-2016, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T00:39:09-07:00","id":930227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=929943#post929943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Wyrdhamster's argument was misread. He claims that since Seers have counterparts of most Legacies, specifically stating it is redundant and doesn't look neat on paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly this. From what I get of their Orderbook - Seers have variants in most Legacies, even those with already 'dual Order' in Pentacle. With this, pointing Legacy as 'or Seers' in Parent section is unnecessary, making only false dichotomy of 'only few Legacies are from Seers' - at least this is what I read from <b>Seers of Throne </b>1E book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T01:22:22-07:00","id":930237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=930211#post930211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Guardian Daksha is that it's partially diluted themes of Legacy. Daksha were point made that Mysterium are not 'nice guys' that share knowlegde - it shown they ideology lead to Nazis.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're overthinking things. Knowing Wood, I suspect you're underestimating how closely he associates &quot;Atlanteans&quot; in general with three-eyed blue skinned Nazi hermaphrodites. (See also <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/183575/Chariot-Fantasy-Roleplaying-in-an-Age-of-Miracles\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Chariot</i></a>) White Wolf gave him an opportunity to indulge his Theosophy fascination, and he took it. The morality of the Mysterium is, I suspect, irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","user":"Mr Innes","date":". 07-12-2016, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T09:54:27-07:00","id":930391,"title":"","content":"Has it been mentioned anywhere when we'll get news on the Tremere?<br /> Does Dave have a blog anywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T11:19:21-07:00","id":930431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=930391#post930391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it been mentioned anywhere when we'll get news on the Tremere?</div> </div> </div> </div>After the errata's finalised. Probably after GenCon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T11:27:56-07:00","id":930437,"title":"","content":"As a person who always wanted to play out the &quot;unwilling Tremere&quot; narrative where you are basically a brooding cursed hero who desperately fights against their condition and tries to make a compromise with the curse while trying to find a way out, are these Tremere rules going to make me happy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T20:04:54-07:00","id":930672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=930431#post930431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After the errata's finalised. Probably after GenCon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nice! Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T05:49:02-07:00","id":930801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=929776#post929776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Above lists seems like putting Seers is more: 'We do not have idea what second Pentacle Order would work in this example - Okay, we must put second Order, so it will be Seers'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or things like Guardian Dakasha.<br /> <br /> <b>I'm all for opening format to second Paret Order - but not making it <i>ironclad</i> standard.</b> And not count Seers in it, as from what I understand setting, Seers can almost always have their own version of any Legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean ironclad? One of the ten already breaks that format, so I wouldn't call it ironclad in any way at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T05:54:49-07:00","id":930807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=930801#post930801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean ironclad? One of the ten already breaks that format, so I wouldn't call it ironclad in any way at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>If one of ten is only Singiel Order, I would say we have ironclad. Examples imply that (almost) all Legacies have double Orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T06:09:28-07:00","id":930815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=930807#post930807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If one of ten is only Singiel Order, I would say we have ironclad. Examples imply that (almost) all Legacies have double Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. And that &quot;(almost)&quot; is important, because it means it isn't ironclad. Unless, of course, it's extremely rusty iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T08:01:48-07:00","id":930847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=930431#post930431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After the errata's finalised. Probably after GenCon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope we get updates for the other 1e Legacies mentioned in the corebook. Just started a Mage chronicle, and I'm aiming for my Acanthus th\u00e9arch to join the Walkers in Mists!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T08:07:09-07:00","id":930852,"title":"","content":"It's not too likely that they'll all be updated since it's basically the developers being super nice by throwing us some freebies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T10:06:06-08:00","id":1468695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=929344#post929344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sisterhood of the Blessed (Ladder or Seers / Acanthus)<br /> Eleventh Question (Guardian or Mysterium / Moros) <b>- already in the corebook</b><br /> Perfected Adept (Arrow or Council / Obrimos)<br /> Cryptologos (Council or Mysterium / Mastigos)<br /> Orphans of Proteus (Mysterium or Arrow / Thyrsus)<br /> <br /> The Adepts, Sisterhood and Cryptologos are all back-of-beermat converted already for my own game, as they're the Legacies my players' characters have taken. The Redoubtable Neall Raemonn Price is working up the Orphans as a hobby project.<br /> <br /> Bonus round, for if we find ourselves overburdened with time, will be:<br /> <br /> House of Ariadne (Mysterium or Seers / Acanthus)<br /> Forge Masters (Arrow or Council / Moros)<br /> Clavicularius / Bene Ashmedai (Ladder or Seers / Mastigos)<br /> Dreamspeakers (Council / Thyrsus)<br /> Daksha (Mysterium or Guardian / Obrimos)<br /> <br /> Although they will have to wait until after Signs of Sorcery comes out - the Clavicularius and Forge Masters in particular have Attainments based on spells from that book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Greetings,<br /> <br /> A bit of necromancy, but any idea when and if those Legacies are getting updated? Either in official products or a blog post? Only the <b>House of Ariadn</b>e was updated in Nameless and Accursed, and I am dying to see <b>Bene Ashmedai</b> (best Legacy ever).<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}